# The corpus database is derived and never committed. What readers are served is
# the JSON in web/data/ that export_json.py writes -- the same split
# was-it-true and pubfig-content use. A gate that needed the DB would need the
# network, and a builder has neither.
whocitedit.db
harvest/raw/
harvest/manifest.jsonl
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
web/node_modules/
web/app/node_modules/
web/app/dist/
# The rendered site. This was tracked for the repository's first four commits
# because .gitignore carried `web/out/` -- the Next.js output directory, from a
# plan that was abandoned before the first render -- and never the directory the
# Python renderer actually writes. It doubled the checkout, put 9,916 generated
# files into every diff, and left rendered HTML hand-editable by a builder.
web/site/
